# The docs-refresh component's directories (H7.10a).
# homelab-docs-refresh.service runs `systemd-tmpfiles --create` on this file in ExecStartPre=
# with the `+` prefix, which runs that one command as root while the service itself runs as
# {{ sys_user }}. systemd-tmpfiles-setup.service also creates both directories at boot. dpkg never
# owns a path under /home.
#
# The first line is docs' hostPath. The docs Deployment (ansible/roles/k8s/docs) mounts it as
# `type: Directory`, so it must exist before the pod starts on a rebuilt daniel-box: a missing path
# leaves the pod in ContainerCreating. kubelet would create it as root, and the build runs as
# {{ sys_user }}. Its path equals `docs_host_site_dir` in ansible/roles/k8s/docs/defaults/main.yml
# (ansible/tests/setup/test_docs_refresh_site_dir.py holds the two equal).
#
# The second line is the commit-failure stamp directory. It sits outside the checkout because an
# untracked file inside it parks the deployer. /var/lib/homelab is root-owned 0755.
#Type Path                                Mode User          Group         Age
d /home/{{ sys_user }}/docs-site          0755 {{ sys_user }} {{ sys_user }} -
d /var/lib/homelab/docs-refresh.d         0755 {{ sys_user }} {{ sys_user }} -
